The US has had the ICC on its radar more or less throughout the second Trump term Image: John Thys/AFP Advertisement
US President Donald Trump 's administration imposed sanctions on the International Criminal Court (ICC) &#160;on Friday, hours after one of its former judges won the Nobel Peace Prize.&#160;
This comes as the US has in recent months made no bones about pursuing what Secretary of State Marco Rubio has called a "sweeping campaign to dismantle the threat posed by the International Criminal Court."
The United States and Israel had both strongly opposed the court's arrest warrants for top Israeli officials, including Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu .
Since 2020 and the back end of Trump's first term, the US had also opposed investigations into military actions in Afghanistan that "deprioritize" alleged US wrongdoings, focusing on the Taliban,&#160;but can nevertheless include them.
